body:
If a caller does `mongo.Connect(nil)`, `opts` becomes `[]*options.ClientOptions{nil}` and `opt.Monitor` dereferences a nil pointer here (the trampoline's recover will swallow the panic, but the monitor is then never injected). A small guard keeps the hook robust:

```go
for _, opt := range opts {
    if opt == nil {
        continue
    }
    if opt.Monitor == nil {
        opt.SetMonitor(monitor)
    }
}
```

Same pattern exists in the v1 hook, so feel free to treat this as optional here.

